[Better Approach] - Sorting and Two Pointer - O(mn Log n + mn2) Time and O(1) SpaceThe idea is to sort each row, then for each row select an element, and use two pointers to find the required pair in the other rows.Steps:Sort all the rows in ascending order. The time complexity for this preprocessing will be O(m x n log n).Now we select each row one by one and find pair elements in the remaining rows after the current row.Take two iterators, left and right. left iterator points left corner of the current i'th row and right iterator points right corner of the next j'th row in which we are going to find a pair of elements.If mat[i][left] + mat[j][right] < sum then left++ i.e; move in i'th row towards the right corner, otherwise right++ i.e; move in j'th row towards the left corner
